## The red this change carries and does not cause

`driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile` is red on the base commit `ae2373cb` itself, and this change is not why:
the diff touches neither `tools/loop/layout.tsv`, `tools/loop/report.sh` nor `tools/loop/state.sh`
(`git diff --name-only HEAD` is the 8 files of the fix, and no `tools/loop/*.sh` is among them), and
`git show ae2373cb:tools/loop/layout.tsv | grep -n 'action_add\|cmd_publish_refused'` exits 1 — the base's own
`layout.tsv` owns neither function. The case reports two rows:

    report.sh defines action_add and its row does not own it
    state.sh defines cmd_publish_refused and its row does not own it

It is no `policy#*` case, and the only case file this change edits (`tools/loop/tests/loop-cases.sh`) is green in
both other selections above. Carried, not caused here.
